peer_feedback_assignment_1:
  issue_number: 58
  issue_owner: anapau-tapia
  issue_ok: no
  issue_status: Could not locate your AI Usage Statement - No '.callout-note' block.
  overall_comments:
    positive: The submission has a clear, uncluttered formatting theme.
    negative: |-
      The submission requires further context on the responses given.
      The submission is missing some tasks.
    advice: |-
      In order for the callout-note to render, the submission needs ```{r} before the note and ``` after.
      It would be good to use a pattern for how headers are used in the rendered document, e.g. sections are given a large header while questions have a small header to clearly divide up the document. This will help make it easier for readers to follow and will give it some "flow".
  scores:
    Written Communication:
      score: 3.0
      comment: The only writting included in the submission is a short introduction
        and then some findings detail in the Task 5 responses.
    Project Skeleton:
      score: 3.0
      comment: Tasks 6 and 7 are skipped and there is no rendered AI usage statement.
    Tables & Document Presentation:
      score: 3.0
      comment: The tables that were included are presented fine, but there are two
        tables missing.
    Data Visualization:
      score: 0.0
      comment: There are no visualizations included in this submission to review.
    Exploratory Data Analysis:
      score: 10.0
      comment: DEFAULT SCORE
    Code Quality:
      score: 4.0
      comment: For the code that is included in the submission, it is labeled and
        easy to follow. However, it appears that some incorrect answers may be given
        from the code used.
    Data Preparation:
      score: 10.0
      comment: DEFAULT SCORE
    Analysis and Findings:
      score: 2.0
      comment: There are very few analyses and findings provided in the submission.
        There is limited analysis provided in the tables that are included from Task
        5.
    Extra Credit:
      score: 0.0
      comment: Not completed
  mp_number: 2.0
peer_feedback_assignment_2:
  issue_number: 59
  issue_owner: miggonzalz
  issue_ok: yes
  issue_status: OK
  overall_comments:
    positive: The flow of the final insights task is nice, easy to read, and has good
      visuals.
    negative: I'd suggest either hiding or excluding descriptive statistics from the
      rendered document. They take up a lot of room and hinder the flow of the overall
      report.
    advice: Either include a dropdown to view initial statistics or exclude from the
      rendered document.
  scores:
    Written Communication:
      score: 6.0
      comment: The key finds are there and are not difficult to discern, but there
        are some grammatical errors.
    Project Skeleton:
      score: 7.0
      comment: All tasks are completed without any minor flaws.
    Tables & Document Presentation:
      score: 8.0
      comment: Tables are well formatted and easy to read, with nice titles and descriptions.
    Data Visualization:
      score: 6.0
      comment: The label for the values on the x axis for Task 6 Q1 could be improved.
        Using [15,20] to denote an age group randing from 15-20 years old is not immediately
        apparent to the reader. Additionally, I would suggest removing sleeping as
        an activity in the graph for Q2. Most people are spending 7-9 hours sleeping
        per day, so including this activity distorts what people are doing during
        the summer months.
    Exploratory Data Analysis:
      score: 10.0
      comment: DEFAULT SCORE
    Code Quality:
      score: 8.0
      comment: Code is clear with comments explaining what is being accomplished with
        each block.
    Data Preparation:
      score: 10.0
      comment: DEFAULT SCORE
    Analysis and Findings:
      score: 8.0
      comment: The report has clear findings explained for the three groups along
        with a nice graphic that demonstrates where each demographic is at in four
        major categories.
    Extra Credit:
      score: 6.0
      comment: The submission includes both a completed data relationship diagram
        and a ring visualization to use in the app.
  mp_number: 2.0
peer_feedback_assignment_3:
  issue_number: 60
  issue_owner: maryononye
  issue_ok: yes
  issue_status: OK
  overall_comments:
    positive: This submission has good written context that helps the reader understand
      what is being accomplished.
    negative: To exclude code blocks from the rendered document.
    advice: Exclude code blocks from rendered document.
  scores:
    Written Communication:
      score: 8.0
      comment: The submission has thorough context for each assigned task, making
        it easy to follow through the report.
    Project Skeleton:
      score: 7.0
      comment: The submission has all provided tasks completed satisfactorily. Responses
        are thorough.
    Tables & Document Presentation:
      score: 4.0
      comment: It is difficult to locate tables in the rendered document because code
        blocks are included in the rendered document, visually taking up more space
        than the tables themselves.
    Data Visualization:
      score: 6.0
      comment: Data visualizations could have used color to make them more "publication"
        ready.
    Exploratory Data Analysis:
      score: 10.0
      comment: DEFAULT SCORE
    Code Quality:
      score: 7.0
      comment: Code is easy to follow, but comments walking through what is being
        accomplished did not necessarily need to be rendered. Additionally, it is
        distracting including code blocks in the rendered document.
    Data Preparation:
      score: 10.0
      comment: DEFAULT SCORE
    Analysis and Findings:
      score: 7.0
      comment: Analysis is thorough, but data could be presented in a more succinct
        way, particularly by combining all data into a single table.
    Extra Credit:
      score: 0.0
      comment: No extra credit tasks were completed.
  mp_number: 2.0
evaluator: mclycke

